;; ../../../../spec-concrete/5.04-typing-relation.watsup:6.1-9.94
relation Eval_static: p, TC, (expressionIR # (( _typeIR'' _ctk'' )))

1. Case analysis on `expressionIR`
  1. Case `expressionIR` has type `booleanLiteral`
    1. Let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR` as `booleanLiteral`
    2. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean: p, TC, (`booleanLiteral` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Case analysis on `booleanLiteral`
        1. Case `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`
          1. Result in ``(b true)` as `value``

        2. Case `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`
          1. Result in ``(b false)` as `value``

  2. Case `expressionIR` has type `numberLiteral`
    1. Let `numberLiteral` be `expressionIR` as `numberLiteral`
    2. Group literalExpressionIR-number: p, TC, (`numberLiteral` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Case analysis on `numberLiteral`
        1. Case `numberLiteral` matches pattern `D%`
          1. Let `(d i)` be numberLiteral
          2. Result in ``(d i)` as `value``

        2. Case `numberLiteral` matches pattern `%W%`
          1. Let `(n w i)` be numberLiteral
          2. Result in ``(n w i)` as `value``

        3. Case `numberLiteral` matches pattern `%S%`
          1. Let `(n s i)` be numberLiteral
          2. Result in ``(n s i)` as `value``

  3. Case `expressionIR` has type `stringLiteral`
    1. Let `(" text ")` be `expressionIR` as `stringLiteral`
    2. Group literalExpressionIR-stringliteral: p, TC, (`(" text ")` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Result in ``(" text ")` as `value``

  4. Case `expressionIR` has type `prefixedNameIR`
    1. Let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR` as `prefixedNameIR`
    2. Group referenceExpression: p, TC, (`prefixedNameIR` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Let `value` be `$find_value(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`
      2. Result in `value`

  5. Case `expressionIR` has type `defaultExpression`
    1. Let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR` as `defaultExpression`
    2. Group defaultExpressionIR: p, TC, (`(...)` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Result in ``(default)` as `value``

  6. Case `expressionIR` has type `unaryExpressionIR`
    1. Let `(unop typedExpressionIR)` be `expressionIR` as `unaryExpressionIR`
    2. Group unaryExpressionIR: p, TC, (`(unop typedExpressionIR)` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Case analysis on `unop`
        1. Case `unop` matches pattern `~`
          1. Let [`value` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Result in ``$un_bnot(value)``

        2. Case `unop` matches pattern `!`
          1. Let [`value` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Result in ``$un_lnot(value)``

        3. Case `unop` matches pattern `+`
          1. Let [`value` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Result in ``$un_plus(value)``

        4. Case `unop` matches pattern `-`
          1. Let [`value` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Result in ``$un_minus(value)``

  7. Case `expressionIR` has type `binaryExpressionIR`
    1. Let `(typedExpressionIR_l binop typedExpressionIR_r)` be `expressionIR` as `binaryExpressionIR`
    2. Group binaryExpressionIR: p, TC, (`(typedExpressionIR_l binop typedExpressionIR_r)` as `expressionIR` # (( _typeIR _ctk )))

      1. Case analysis on `binop`
        1. Case `binop` matches pattern `+`
          1. Let [`value_l` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR_l`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Let [`value_r` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR_r`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          3. Result in ``$bin_plus(value_l, value_r)``

        2. Case `binop` matches pattern `|+|`
          1. Let [`value_l` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR_l`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          2. Let [`value_r` be the static evaluation of `typedExpressionIR_r`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`](Eval_static)
          3. Result in ``$bin_satplus(value_l, value_r)``

