        2. Group tupleKeysetExpression-range: TC, TBLC, `(( expression_l .. expression_r ))` as `keysetExpression`

          1. Assert that (|TBLC.keys| = 1).
            1. (TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok: TC TBLC (nolpm) |- TBLC.keys @ [(expression_l .. expression_r)] : TBLS simpleKeysetExpressionIR'*)
            2. Assert that simpleKeysetExpressionIR'* matches pattern [ _/1 ].
              1. Let `[simpleKeysetExpressionIR]` be simpleKeysetExpressionIR'*
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

      3. Case `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `(DEFAULT)`
        1. Group tupleKeysetExpression-default: TC, TBLC, `((default))` as `keysetExpression`

          1. Let `matchMode` be TBLC.mode
          2. Assert that matchMode matches pattern `NOPRILPM%`.
            1. Let `(noprilpm n)` be matchMode
            2. Let `TBLS` be (lpm n)
            3. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(default)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``
          3. Case analysis on `TBLC.mode`
            1. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `NOPRI`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(default)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

            2. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `PRI`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(default)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

            3. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `PRILPM`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(default)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

      4. Case `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `(_)`
        1. Group tupleKeysetExpression-dontcare: TC, TBLC, `((_))` as `keysetExpression`

          1. Let `matchMode` be TBLC.mode
          2. Assert that matchMode matches pattern `NOPRILPM%`.
            1. Let `(noprilpm n)` be matchMode
            2. Let `TBLS` be (lpm 0)
            3. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(_)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``
          3. Case analysis on `TBLC.mode`
            1. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `NOPRI`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(_)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

            2. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `PRI`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(_)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

            3. Case `TBLC.mode` matches pattern `PRILPM`
              1. Let `TBLS` be (nolpm)
              2. Result in `TBLS`, ``(( [(_)] ))` as `keysetExpressionIR``

